# No exit codes in operator documentation

Never mention exit codes, process-status numbers (`0`/`1`/`2`/`3` as command results), or `echo $?`
in operator documentation: `docs/`, `README.md`, `SUPPORT.md`, and new `CHANGELOG.md` entries.

There is no `docs/reference/exit-codes.md`. Do not recreate it. Do not add Exit tables to command
pages.

Operators read the **verdict** on the report (clean / infected / suspicious / error / rotation
unsafe / in place / unknown). CI still gates on process status — that contract lives in code, tests,
and skills, never in operator docs.

Historical changelog sections already shipped may keep their wording.
